<title>JAPAN: Japan March copper imports down 3.8 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan March copper imports down 3.8 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined copper imports in March totalled 20,761 tonnes, down 3.8 percent from 21,579 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Monday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Mar 97	  Feb 97	 Mar 96</p>
<p> Total	    20,761	  23,756	 21,579</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Chile	    10,616	  12,869	  6,409</p>
<p> U.S.		1,919	   2,523	  5,967</p>
<p> Zambia		891	   1,052	  1,042</p>
<p>Imports in the first three months of calendar 1997 were 72,041 tonnes, up from 67,636 tonnes during the same period last year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
